# SSSF environment. Copy to .env at the target repo root and fill in.
#
# WHICH KEYS YOU NEED DEPENDS ON YOUR ROSTER.
# Every `model:` in adws/adw_sssf_config/sssf.config.yaml is written as
# provider/model-id. The provider half decides which key must be set, and which
# key pi reads for that provider comes from ~/.pi/agent/models.json.
#
# The starter roster names ONE provider on purpose — `ollama-cloud/kimi-k2.7-code`
# on `defaults.model`, inherited by every agent, overridden by none — so there is
# exactly one credential to have working before the first run, and none of the
# lines below may need to be set at all: a provider registered in
# ~/.pi/agent/models.json can carry its own `apiKey` (a literal, or a script pi
# shells for it), in which case pi authenticates it and `.env` never sees a key.
#
# Set a key here only for a provider whose entry in that file reads one from the
# environment. The commented names are the ones a roster reaches for most often —
# uncomment the one your own `model:` lines actually name.
#
# Nothing validates this for you. `agents.validate()` checks that a model is
# written as provider/id, not that the provider is reachable or that its key is
# set, so a missing key shows up when that agent runs, not at startup.

# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# XAI_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Optional overrides
# PI_PATH=pi                       # pi binary if not on PATH
# PI_MODELS_PATH=~/.pi/agent/models.json
# ENGINEER_NAME=                   # engineer lane label, defaults to git user.name
